  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1041 PM MDT Thu Jul 9 2026\n\nHigh pressure will shift east slightly closer to the area on Friday \nbefore shifting to the Four Corners on Saturday. High pressure then \npushes northward over the northern Plains and Rockies then expands \nand strengthens Sunday. This will allow for east flow at the upper \nlevels and will help flush in some tropical moisture. Expect daily \nthunderstorm chances focusing over the area mountains with more \nisolated activity in the lowlands. Monday and Tuesday the high \npressure will flatten over a good portion of the northern CONUS \nallowing for a good tap of moisture to push in during this time. PW \nvalues will be above average during this time with values of 1.2-\n1.3\" which will add to the flooding threat with storms and may also \nadd to the coverage of thunderstorms across the area.",
